  "notes": [
    "Regional site overlay (ADR 0042) for Paide / Wittenstein (Weissenstein), May 1343: the Order commandery castle, its outer bailey, ditch, the small chartered town and its fields.",
    "Coordinates are metres from the origin (the castle keep area), x east, y south. Every id is prefixed paide. (ADR 0042 section 5).",
    "Castle layout after the plan in Borowski (2010) from K. von Loewis of Menar and A. Tuulse (1942), summarised at medievalheritage.eu: square upper ward with a wide north wing (chapel, chapter house) and a narrow east wing (refectory), the octagonal keep in the south-west corner of the upper ward, an outer bailey to the south and west, a west gatehouse in front of a wide ditch and a north-east gate tower. The 1343 building phase of each part is unverified (raised to a commandery early in the 14th c.).",
    "OSM supplies only the keep position (way 596093616, 'Pikk Hermann'); modern Paide streets, buildings, ponds and park paths are not used. Roads, houses and fields are overlay records with confidence labels.",
    "The modern name 'Pikk Hermann' (Tall Hermann) is not attested for 1343; the plan calls it the keep. It is not the Toompea tower of the same name (docs/LOCATIONS/paide_castle.md)."
  ],
